<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0012/e_0042> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/ExtractedEntity> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0012/e_0024> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/Drug> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/AnatomyEntity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0012/tu_0003> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Documentation of the type and dose of nutraceutical products used by patients with HF is recommended. (Strength of Evidence = C) Nutraceutical use is not recommended for relief of symptomatic HF or for the secondary prevention of cardiovascular events. Patients should be instructed to avoid using natural or synthetic products containing ephedra (ma huang), ephedrine, or its metabolites because of an increase risk of mortality and morbidity. Products should be avoided that may have significant drug interactions with digoxin, vasodilators, beta blockers, antiarrhythmic drugs, and anticoagulants. (Strength of Evidence = B)" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0012/na_0015> <http://digistrucmed.org/deonticForce> "ADVISORY" .
